{"name":"Spare White","hex":"#e4e4dd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spare","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extra.\nBeing more than what is necessary, or what must be used or reserved; not wanted, or not used; superfluous.","Being more than what is necessary, or what must be used or reserved; not wanted, or not used; superfluous."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of sparing; moderation; restraint.","Parsimony; frugal use."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spare"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spare (memoir)","blocks":[{"text":"Spare is a memoir by Prince Harry, Duke of Sussex, which was released in 2023. It was ghostwritten by J. R. Moehringer and published by Penguin Random House. An audiobook edition is narrated by Harry."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/69/Spare_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spare_(memoir)","wikidata":"Q114892138"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/First_Lady_Barbara_Bush_greets_Prince_William_at_the_Winfield_House_in_1991.jpg/500px-First_Lady_Barbara_Bush_greets_Prince_William_at_the_Winfield_House_in_1991.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/First_Lady_Barbara_Bush_greets_Prince_William_at_the_Winfield_House_in_1991.jpg/1280px-First_Lady_Barbara_Bush_greets_Prince_William_at_the_Winfield_House_in_1991.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/First_Lady_Barbara_Bush_greets_Prince_William_at_the_Winfield_House_in_1991.jpg/500px-First_Lady_Barbara_Bush_greets_Prince_William_at_the_Winfield_House_in_1991.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Harry (right) aged six, meeting Barbara Bush alongside his brother William and mother Diana","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFirst_Lady_Barbara_Bush_greets_Prince_William_at_the_Winfield_House_in_1991.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Half_price_copies_of_the_Prince_Harry_memoir_Spare_in_W._H._Smith_London_14_Jan_2023.jpg/500px-Half_price_copies_of_the_Prince_Harry_memoir_Spare_in_W._H._Smith_London_14_Jan_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Half_price_copies_of_the_Prince_Harry_memoir_Spare_in_W._H._Smith_London_14_Jan_2023.jpg/1280px-Half_price_copies_of_the_Prince_Harry_memoir_Spare_in_W._H._Smith_London_14_Jan_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_co